1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,032
The better question was announced in parliament and then repeated in a conversation on the steps: who decides what a household needs?

2
00:00:08,032 --> 00:00:13,391
“We prefer to ask how much water is missing,” the member said.

3
00:00:13,391 --> 00:00:24,044
“We should ask who is entitled to it.” The launch of the new tariff was, ultimately, a launch of a different question.

4
00:00:24,044 --> 00:00:28,558
The strange part was how little it took to convince the room.

5
00:00:28,558 --> 00:00:34,641
“You can devise a rate that corresponds to a real bill,” the economist said.

6
00:00:34,641 --> 00:00:46,809
“A proposition with a definite number beats a certainty with none.” The contradiction at the heart of the old system was that it was both conclusive and wasteful.

7
00:00:46,809 --> 00:00:52,648
“We proclaim validity and we cannot verify the meter,” the clerk said.

8
00:00:52,648 --> 00:01:08,999
“We infer mastery from a conquest of paperwork.” The generosity of the old exemption was, in fact, economical only for the rich, and anyhow nobody had ever checked the verification.

9
00:01:08,999 --> 00:01:14,718
The final draft was shorter by half, and its permanence was the point.

10
00:01:14,718 --> 00:01:22,966
“A rule that survives a change of government is worth more than a rule that sucks up the whole budget,” the chair said.

11
00:01:22,966 --> 00:01:29,800
“We have hidden behind a falsehood: that a complicated form is a fair one.”

12
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:33,844
The inducement to cheat was the exemption itself.

13
00:01:33,844 --> 00:01:38,708
“Where there is hiding, there is a lie,” Maya wrote.

14
00:01:38,708 --> 00:01:51,425
“Where there is a definite limit, there is a defensible argument.” The missing element was not money but room: a level at which a poor household could still pay.

15
00:01:51,425 --> 00:01:59,433
The invitation to the public was issued under the new rule, and the first question at the meeting was the better one.

16
00:01:59,433 --> 00:02:10,261
The end of the session, the government and the market on the same page, the result of the whole period: a question about need rather than about price.

17
00:02:10,261 --> 00:02:22,333
The adventure of the launch was that it could fail; the final conversation, the strange proposition, and the missing number all had to correspond to something real.

18
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:29,691
We would rather be conclusive than generous, and ultimately that was the inducement we had to remove.

19
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:33,760
Then the parliament would announce the figure publicly.

20
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:47,562
If we now validate the rule, we can show the party that the law, the interest, and the policy are on the right side; it would be contradictory to attain permanence without an infinity of patience.

21
00:02:47,562 --> 00:02:54,225
The social world and the state would have to agree before the level changed.
